@startuml
!theme plain
title Queue Job Recovery — All Failure Scenarios

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #343a40
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #fff3cd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #e8f4fd

|Worker|
start

:Job dequeued from Redis;
:AcquireLock + MarkStarted;
:Start heartbeat goroutine\n(renews every 10 min, TTL 20 min);
:Processor.Process(ctx, payload);

|Failure Mode|

if (How did the job stop?) then

  |Graceful Shutdown|
  :Server receives SIGINT (Ctrl+C);
  note right
    **Recovery: INSTANT on next boot**
    ──────────────────────────────
    Worker detects ctx.Err() != nil
    → Skips MarkFailed
    → Deletes heartbeat
    → Releases lock
    → Job stays "processing"

    On next boot:
    RecoverOnStartup() finds job
    in "processing" with no heartbeat
    → re-enqueues immediately
  end note
  :Job stays **processing**\n(heartbeat deleted, lock released);
  :Server restarts;
  :RecoverOnStartup → re-enqueue;
  #palegreen:Job re-processed from scratch;
  stop

else
  |Hard Crash|
  if (Restart timing?) then

    |Restart > 20 min after crash|
    :Heartbeat TTL expired in Redis;
    note right
      **Recovery: INSTANT on boot**
      ──────────────────────────
      Heartbeat expired naturally
      (Redis TTL = 20 min)

      RecoverOnStartup() finds job
      in "processing" with no heartbeat
      → ForceReleaseLock
      → MarkPendingIfProcessing
      → re-enqueue
    end note
    :Server restarts;
    :RecoverOnStartup → re-enqueue;
    #palegreen:Job re-processed from scratch;
    stop

  else (Restart < 20 min after crash)
    :Heartbeat still alive in Redis;
    note right
      **Recovery: up to 2 hours**
      ──────────────────────────
      RecoverOnStartup() sees heartbeat
      → thinks worker is alive → skips

      After 20 min: heartbeat TTL expires

      Periodic recovery (every 10 min)
      checks: startedAt > **2 hours** (lockTTL)
      AND no heartbeat → re-enqueue

      Worst case: 2 hours + 10 min

      **Future improvement:** reduce
      threshold to heartbeatTTL (20 min)
      → worst case becomes ~30 min
    end note
    :Server restarts;
    :RecoverOnStartup → skipped\n(heartbeat still alive);
    :Wait for heartbeat TTL to expire\n(up to 20 min);
    :Periodic recovery waits until\njob age > lockTTL (2 hours);
    :ForceReleaseLock + re-enqueue;
    #palegreen:Job re-processed from scratch;
    stop

  endif

endif

|Summary|

note
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  **Recovery Timeline Summary**
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  | Scenario                      | Recovery Time    |
  |-------------------------------|------------------|
  | Graceful shutdown (Ctrl+C)    | Instant on boot  |
  | Hard crash, restart > 20 min  | Instant on boot  |
  | Hard crash, restart < 20 min  | Up to 2 hours    |
  | User cancellation             | No recovery      |
  |   (terminal state)            |   (by design)    |

  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  **Key Constants**
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  • heartbeatTTL    = 20 min (Redis key auto-expire)
  • heartbeatInterval = 10 min (renewal frequency)
  • lockTTL         = 2 hours (lock expiration)
  • recoveryGrace   = 2 min (skip newly started jobs)
  • periodicInterval = 10 min (recovery check cycle)

  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  **Recovery Mechanisms**
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  1. RecoverOnStartup — runs once on boot
     Catches: stale processing jobs (no heartbeat)

  2. Periodic recovery — runs every 10 min
     Catches: jobs running > 20 min with no heartbeat
     (covers: quick restart after crash, zombie workers)

  3. Lock steal — worker-initiated
     Catches: live system where lock holder died
     (worker checks heartbeat of lock holder)
end note

@enduml
